cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Effective Resistance as an Inverse Descriptor of Random Geometric Networks
message: If you use this software or data, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Costa
    given-names: Jefferson Carlos Lima da
    affiliation: Centro de Informática, Universidade Federal de Pernambuco
abstract: >-
  Simulation and analysis code for an MSc dissertation on charge transport in
  random conductive-stick networks. Builds random 2D and 3D stick networks,
  solves the percolating cluster as a resistor network through the graph
  Laplacian, studies how effective resistance depends on stick number, stick
  length and film thickness, and tests whether an onion-layer probe protocol
  recovers geometric information that a single scalar resistance measurement
  collapses away.
keywords:
  - percolation
  - effective resistance
  - stick networks
  - nanowire networks
  - graph Laplacian
  - inverse problem
license: MIT
year: 2026
